After elastic collision,

\begin{aligned}
v_A^{\prime} & =\left(\frac{m-2 m}{m+2 m}\right)(9)+\frac{2(2 m)}{m+2 m}(0) \\
& =-3 \mathrm{~ms}^{-1}
\end{aligned}

Now from conservation of linear momentum after all collisions are complete,

\begin{array}{rlrl}
m\left(+9 \mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\right) & =m\left(-3 \mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\right)+3 m\left(v_C\right) \\
& \text { or } \quad v_C & =4 \mathrm{~ms}^{-1}
\end{array}

$y_{C M}$
\begin{gathered}
=\frac{m_1 y_1+m_2 y_2+m_3 y_3+m_4 y_4+m_5 y_5}{m_1+m_2+m_3+m_4+m_5} \\
=\frac{(6 m)(0)+(m)(a)+m(a)+m(0)}{6 m+m+m+m+m}=\frac{a}{10}
\end{gathered}

Between $A$ and $B$, height fallen by block $h_1=\sqrt{3} \tan 60^{\circ}=3 \mathrm{~m}$.
$\therefore$ speed of block just before striking the second incline,

v_1=\sqrt{2 g h_1}=\sqrt{2 \times 10 \times 3}=\sqrt{60} \mathrm{~ms}^{-1}
